+
+## Quiz content transfer
+
+- `GET /moderate/quizzes/{id}/export` renders the only `<pre>` on the page.
+  `GET /moderate/quizzes/import` renders the import form; POST to that same path
+  parses `quiz_json` and redirects to the newly created quiz. Both are covered by
+  moderator authentication; POST also uses the existing CSRF token.
+- `transfer::QuizContents` is the portable DTO: only `title` and `questions`.
+  Questions use `QuestionInput` (`text`, `active`, `options`), and options use
+  `Choice` (`text`, `correct`). No database IDs or preview/runtime state can be
+  serialized through it. Database reads explicitly order questions and options.
+- Required JSON fields must have the stated types. Only omitted `active` and
+  `correct` fields get defaults (`true` and `false` respectively); `null`, strings,
+  and numbers are not coerced into booleans. Explicit object-shape checks prevent
+  Serde from accepting positional arrays as structs. Unknown fields are ignored
+  on import and never exported. Empty quizzes are allowed; blank titles are not.
+- Validation calls the same `QuestionInput::errors()` as the question form, and
+  both paths share database insertion and `saved_options()` normalization. Text
+  is trimmed, blank option rows are skipped, and at least two remaining options
+  and one remaining correct choice are required. Errors identify question numbers.
+- The entire JSON document is parsed and validated before any database write.
+  The quiz and every question/option are then inserted in one SQLite transaction;
+  database failure rolls everything back. Titles are not deduplicated. There is
+  no schema change for this feature.
+- Export JSON and retained textarea contents are HTML-escaped, so embedded
+  `</pre>`, `</textarea>`, script tags, ampersands, and Unicode stay copyable text.
+- Tests: `cargo test --offline` includes a trigger-induced failure on the last
+  option to verify transaction rollback, exact output keys/order/defaults, and
+  malformed schemas. `tests/import_export.py` covers HTTP transfers and atomic
+  validation failures. `tests/import_export_browser.py` uses actual Chromium
+  navigation and text insertion to verify copying from the `<pre>`, pasting into
+  the labeled textarea, importing twice, error retention, and mobile layout.
+  `tests/persistence.py` also verifies imported contents across process restarts.
